    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Aidan Daly Auctioneers.... are delighted to introduce to the market this rare opportunity to acquire No. 74, Prospect Avenue, Glasnevin, Dublin 9. Wonderfully positioned with a superb address, this two-bedroom end of terrace cottage dating back to circa 1840 is tucked into this historic and highly desirable enclave in the heart of Old Glasnevin. Needing refurbishment but valued accordingly No.74 offers a wonderful opportunity to create a modern spacious home with huge potential going forward and a substantial attic space.\r\n\r\n*VACANT PROPERTY REFURBISHMENT GRANT; As the property has been vacant for more than two years an application for the government’s vacant homes grant could be applied for which is subject to application and criteria. Prospective purchasers will need to make their own enquiries regarding their eligibility regarding same.\r\nhttps://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-housing-local-government-and-heritage/services/vacant-property-refurbishment-grant/ *\r\n\r\nThe location and convenience of this property is exceptional, nestled in one of Glasnevin's most tranquil and mature settings where you can enjoy every conceivable amenity on your doorstep. It is situated within walking distance of the National Botanic Gardens, Glasnevin Cemetery, Mobhi Road(Na Fianna GAA), Bon Secours Hospital and Dublin City University Campus. This property is next to a myriad of speciality shops, cafes, convenience stores, pubs, gym, churches, and various restaurants. There is a wide selection of creches, pre-schools, primary and secondary schools to choose from. There are a wealth of sporting clubs and social amenities within this area. Numerous bus routes run along Botanic Road and the M1/M50, Dublin Airport, Beaumont & Mater Hospital and city centre are all easily accessible.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises of a bright hallway leading to a spacious lounge with open fireplace (coal effect gas fire) and d/g sliding doors to sunny private rear walled garden. Extended kitchen cum breakfast room. Two generous sized bedrooms each with built in wardrobes. Bathroom with walk in shower and ceramic floor & wall tiling. Gas fired radiator central heating. Double glazed windows and doors throughout. Two garden sheds. Viewing highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall:                                             double glazed pvc door          ceramic floor tile                         carpet      \r\n\r\nLounge:                                 3.58m. x 3.51m.                    carpet         open fireplace  coal effect gas fire         d/g sliding door to rear garden\r\n\r\nKitchen/Breakfast Room:      5.51m. x 2.25m.                  fully fitted units                vinyl       \r\n                                                                                                                                    \r\nBedroom 1  :                          3. 58m. x 3.00m.                                carpet                           built in wardrobe\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:                            3.55m. x 3.13m.                                carpet                           built in wardrobe\r\n\r\nBathroom/ w/c:                       3.38m. x 2.74m.              walk in shower            ceramic floor and wall tile   w/c    whb.  hot press\r\n\r\nRear Garden:                                     walled                two storage sheds"
      },
